<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Hyundai plans $1.4 bln UK chip plant.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Hyundai plans $1.4 bln UK chip plant.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hyundai Electronics, a unit of South Korea's Hyundai Group, said on Tuesday it planned a US$1.4 billion semiconductor plant in Dunfermline, Scotland.</p>
<p>The plant would begin commercial production of dynamic random access memory (DRAM) chips in December 1998 and generate around 1,000 jobs, the company said.</p>
</text>
